    "ls|LS16_S8_U_140": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 140 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.04.2016 \nRanking Framework \n†140. SHRI BHANU PRATAP SINGH VERMA: \nSHRI B. VINOD KUMAR: \nSHRI GUTHA SUKENDER REDDY: \nSHRI ANTO ANTONY: \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has introduced a National Institutions Ranking \nFramework (NIRF) for monitoring the performance of higher educational \ninstitutions in the country; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the salient features of the NIRF; \n(c) whether the Government has excluded Open Universities and certain institutions \nof higher learning from NIRF; \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and \n(e) whether the Government has any plan for including all the institutions of higher \nlearning into the NIRF and if so, the details thereof and the steps taken by the \nGovernment in this regard? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \na) & (b):   Yes, Madam. The National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF)  has been \nlaunched on September 29, 2015 to facilitate benchmarking and comparing the higher \neducational institutions. It would promote competition between the institutions and would \nhelp them to understand their areas of strength and weakness and to take corrective action \nas nec essary. The NIRF has five broad parameters under which educational institutions \nwould be compared and ranked. These pertain to (i) Teaching, Learning and Resources (ii) \nResearch, Projects and Collaborative Performance (iii) Graduation Outcomes (iv) Outreach \nand Inclusivity and (v) Peer and Public Perception. Each of these has several sub -\nparameters, for which a score is computed based  on data supplied by the Institution and \nalso extracted from independent sources. \n(c) & (d):  NIRF is operating in five domains, viz., Universities, Engineering, Management, \nPharmacy and Architecture. The Open Universities have been excluded as their \nperformance cannot be evaluated easily based on the parameters prescribed in NIRF. \n(e): At present there is no such plan. \n \n***** \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_142": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.142\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.4.2016\n \nVAISAKHA 5, 1937 (SAKA)\n \n \nINCREASE IN ENTRY FEE FOR TAJ MAHAL\n \n \n142.\n \nDR. HEENA VIJAYKUMAR GAVIT:\n \nSHRI DHANANJAY MAHADIK:\n \nSHRI MOHITE PATE VIJAYSINH \nSHANKARRAO:\n \nSHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE:\n \nSHRI SATAV RAJEEV:\n \nSHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL:\n \n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Government is planning to increase the entry fee to see the Taj \nMahal\n \nand other centrally protected monuments in the country; \n \n(b)\n \nif so, the details thereof and the reasons for the hike;\n \n(c)\n \nwhether the Government has consulted tourism bodies general public before the \nproposed hike; \n \n(d)\n \nif so, the details thereof and i\nf not the reasons thereof; and\n \n(e)\n \nwhether the Government proposes to introduce a single entry pass for all the \nmonuments in the country to encourage tourists to visit different monuments and \nif so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE, \nCULTURE AND TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) AND \nMINISTER OF STATE, CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n \n(a)\n \nThe entry fee for ticketed monuments including Taj Mahal has been increased \nwith effect from 1.4.2016.\n \n(b)\n \nThe entry fee structure applicable at centrally protected ticketed monuments is \nat Annexure. The entry fee rates were last revised in the year 2001 and \nthereafter no hike was imposed, which was pointed by the Controller and \nAuditor General (CAG) during Per\nformance Audit and recommended for \nrevision of entry fee. \n \n(c)&(d)\n \nBefore effecting the revised rate of entry fee, a preliminary notification was \npublished on 31.7.2015, calling objections/suggestions from all concerned and \nfrom general public.  Before is\nsuing final notification on 31.3.2016, consultation \nwith tour operators and Ministry of Tourism was taken up, in addition \nsuggestions/comments received from individuals were also considered. \n \n(e)\n \nNo such proposal is under consideration. \n \n\n \nANNEXURE \n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 142 FOR 25.4.2016\n \n \nEntry fee Structure at Centrally Protected Ticketed Monuments effective from 1.4.2016\n \n \n \nCategory A\n \n(World Heritage Monuments)\n \n(i) \nCitizen of India and visi\ntors \nfrom SAARC and BIMSTEC \ncountries and overseas citizens of \nIndia\n \nRs.30 per head\n \n(ii) \nOthers (All Nationals other \nthan from countries mentioned \nabove)\n \nRs.500 per h\ne\nad\n \n(iii) \nOthers (as ii above)\n \n*\nRs.750/\n-\n \nper h\ne\nad\n \n \n \nCategory \nB\n \n(Other ticketed \nMonuments)\n \n(i) \nCitizen of India and visitors \nfrom SAARC and BIMSTEC \ncountries and overseas citizens of \nIndia\n \nRs.15/\n-\nper head\n \n(ii) \nOthers (All Nationals other \nthan from countries mentioned \nabove)\n \nRs.\n200/\n-\nper h\ne\nad\n \n(iii) \nOthers (as ii above)\n \n*\nRs.\n30\n0/\n-\n \nper\n \nh\ne\nad\n \n \n \n*\nProvided that the Rs.750/\n-\n \nand Rs.300/\n-\n \nticket is optional for Nationals of countries \nother than mentioned in (i) above. This would entitle the ticket holder to additional \nfacilities as specified by Director General, by order,\n \nfrom\n \ntime to time. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_143": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 143 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.04.2016 \n \nNON-OPERATIVE EPF ACCOUNTS \n \n143. SHRI T. RADHAKRISHNAN: \n        SHRI DHANANJAY MAHADIK: \n        SHRIMATI K. MARAGATHAM: \n        SHRI MOHITE PATIL VIJAYSINH SHANKARRAO: \n        SHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE: \n        DR. HEENA VIJAYKUMAR GAVIT: \n        SHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA: \n        SHRI S. SELVAKUMARA CHINNAYAN: \n \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)the total number of EPF account holders along with the number of \naccounts that are non -operative and corpus involved therein in the \ncountry, State/UT-wise; \n(b)whether the Government proposes to give interest on inoperative PF \naccounts and if so, the details thereof and the number of employees \nlikely to be benefited through this move; and \n(c)the time by which a final decision is likely to be taken in the \nmatter? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI BANDARU DATTATREYA) \n \n(a):            As per Annual Report of Employees’ Provident Fund \nOrganisation (EPFO) for the year 2014 -15, as on 31.03.2015, the \nnumber of Employees’ Provident Fund (EPF) account holders was 15.84 \ncrore. The details relating to number of inoperative accounts is not \nmaintained separately. \nContd..2/- \n  \n\n::  2  :: \n \n \nAs per para 72(6) of the Employees’ Provident Fund Scheme \n1952, certain amounts are classified as ‘Inoperative Accounts’ in \nwhich contributions have not been received for 36 months \ncontinuously. All such Inoperative Accounts have, however, definite \nclaimants.   \n \nAs per Annual Accounts of EPF Organisation, as on 31.03.2015, \nan amount of Rs. 35 ,531.39 crore has been classified as inoperative \naccounts in EPF. \n     \nThe State/UT -wise details of Inoperative Accounts as on 31.03.2015 \nare at Annex.  \n \n(b) & (c): The Central Board of Trustees (CBT), Employees’ Provident \nFund (EPF) in its 212 th meeting held on 29.03.2016 has approved the \nchanges in the definition of inoperative account. However, no proposal \nhas so far been received in the Ministry from EPFO in this regard. \n \n*                                                  ******* \n  \n\n \nANNEX \nANNEX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a)  OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 143 TO BE ANSWERED ON 25.04.2016 BY SHRI T. \nRADHAKRISHNAN, SHRI DHANANJAY MAHADIK,  SHRIMATI K. MARAGATHAM,  \nSHRI MOHITE PATIL VIJAYSINH SHANKARRAO,  SHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE,  DR. \nHEENA VIJAYKUMAR GAVIT,  SHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA,  SHRI S. \nSELVAKUMARA CHINNAYAN REGARDING NON-OPERATIVE EPF ACCOUNTS. \n \nState/UT-wise details of Inoperative Accounts as on 31.03.2015 \n(Amount in Crore) \nS. No. State/UT 2014-15 \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH (includes Telengana) 2,818.59 \n2 BIHAR    247.08 \n3 CHHATTISGARH   358.62 \n4 DELHI 4,259.94 \n5 GOA  187.04 \n6 GUJARAT (includes Daman & Diu and Dadra & Nagar Haveli) 2,425.61 \n7 HARYANA 2,033.14 \n8 HIMACHAL  PRADESH 202.82 \n9 JHARKHAND  354.70 \n10 KARNATAKA 4,610.34 \n11 KERALA (includes Lakshadweep) 414.61 \n12 MADHYA  PRADESH 883.46 \n13 MAHARASHTRA 7,777.01 \n14 North Eastern Regions (Assam, Arunachal Pradesh, Tripura, \nMeghalaya, Nagaland, Manipur & Mizoram)  224.38 \n15 ODISHA 658.94 \n16 PUNJAB (includes Chandigarh) 1,119.63 \n17 RAJASTHAN 503.09 \n18 TAMIL NADU (includes Puducherry) 2,676.12 \n19 UTTARAKHAND 181.86 \n20 UTTAR PRADESH 1,862.28 \n21 WEST BENGAL (includes Sikkim and Andaman & Nicobar Islands) 1,732.13 \n   Total 35,531.39 \n****** ",
