l Nil Nil \nEmployability Enhancement \nTraining Programme (EETP) \nNil 14.53 3.71 \nNational Employability \nEnhancement Mission (NEEM) \nNil Nil Nil \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_165": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION AND LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.165 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.04.2016 \n \n \n MDMS in Rajasthan \n \n  †165. SHRI DEVJI M. PATEL: \n \n Will the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the reasons for delay in releasing the funds by the Government to the tune of Rs. 21.24 \n crores for providing total number of 47000 gas connections under Mid Day Meal \n Scheme (MDMS) in Rajasthan including Jalore-Sirohi district during the year 2014-15; \n \n(b)  the time by which the said amount is likely to be released by the Government; \n \n(c)  whether the Government proposes to provide full contribution to the tribal areas in \n Rajasthan and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d)  whether the Government proposes to allocate an additional amount to Rajasthan for \n payment of foodgrain cost to Food Corporation of India and if so, the details thereof ? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a) & (b):   The Government of Rajasthan had assured before the meeting of the Programme \nApproval Board held on 28.3.2014 that the State would provide funds for \ninstallation of LPG connections in the schools during 2015- 16.  No separate \nCentral assistance was approved for the purpose. \n(c): The funding pattern for Mid Day Meal Scheme had been revised from 1\nst April, \n2015 and the sharing between Centre and States is 60:40 for Rajasthan. There is \nno provision of separate funding pattern for tribal areas.  \n(d): The Central assistance includes the cost of foodgrains to be paid to FCI.   \n******** \n ",
