    "ls|LS16_S8_U_171": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES, \nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*171 \nANSWERED ON 05.05.2016 \n \nREHABILITATION OF DISPLACED FAMILIES DUE TO IRRIGATION PROJECTS  \n†*171.  SHRI RAM TAHAL CHOUDHARY \nSHRI LAXMAN GILUWA \n \nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA \nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has undertaken an assessment of the number of people/families \ndisplaced by irrigation projects in the country including Jharkhand so far, if so, the details \nthereof, State/ project-wise;  \n(b) the number of such people/families rehabilitated as on date and yet to be rehabilitated \nincluding reasons for not rehabilitating all of them; and  \n(c) the steps taken/to be taken by the Government to ensure their proper rehabilitation? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA \nREJUVENATION  \n(SUSHRI UMA BHARTI) \n(a) to (c) \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN  REPLY TO PART S (a) TO (c) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *171. TO BE ANSWERED ON 05.05.2016 IN LOK SABHA \nREGARDING“REHABILITATION OF DISPLACED FAMILIES DUE TO \nIRRIGATION PROJECTS” ASKED BY SHRI RAM TAHAL CHOUDHARY AND \nSHRI LAXMAN GILUWAHON’BLE M.P’s, LOK SABHA: \n \n (a) to (c) Water Resources projects are planned and implemented by the respective State \nGovernments. Further, the concerned State Government and Project Authorities make \nassessment of number of people/families displaced due to such projects and formulate and \nimplement project- wise Rehabilitation and Resettlement (R&R) Plans. To facilitate this \nprocess, Union Government has issued National Rehabilitation and Resettlement  Policy 2007 \n(NRRP-2007) and “Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, \nRehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013” for smooth implementation of R&R action plan in \nrespect of Project Affected Families. However, Compensation for project affected people are \ndecided by the project authorities as per existing R &R policy of Centre/State whichever is \nmore beneficial. \n \nAs per information available with the Central Water Commission (CWC), State -wise and \nproject-wise list of number of displaced persons in respect of Major & Medium Irrigation \nProjects is enclosed.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure as referred to in reply to part (a) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No.171 due for reply on 05.05.2016 regarding \n                                                 Rehabilitation of Displaced Families Due to Irrigation Projects \nProject-wise number of displaced persons in respect of Major & Medium Irrigation Projects \nAndhra Pradesh   \nSl.No. Name of Project Number of displaced people \n1 Srisailam 110097 \n2 Nagarjunasagar 24500 \n3 Yeleru 10121 \n4 Somasila 100000 \n5 Telguganga 16982 \n6 Vamsadhara st-II Hiramandalam(Niradi Barrage) 13622 \n7 Priyadarshini Jurala 8645 \n8 Vengalarasagram 133 \n9 Maddidedda Reservoir 75 \n10 Sriram Sagar 150000 \n11 Annamaya( cheyyeru) 500 \n12 Kandalleru Reservoir 30000 \n TOTAL 464675 \nAssam   \n1 Lower Subansiri H.E. project 443 \n TOTAL 443 \nBihar   \n1 North Koel Reservoir 3368 \n2 Durgavati Reservoir 2500 \n TOTAL 5868 \nChhattisgarh   \n1 Sondur Reservoir( Mahanadi Reservoir) 1516 \n2 Barnal Project 153 \n3 Hasedo Bango ( Mini Mata) 13605 \n4 Kosarteda Medium Irrigationn Project 3695 \n5 Ravi Sankar Sagar Reservir 21495 \n6 Kelo Major 1736 \n7 Dudhawa Reservoir 9437 \n8 Chhirpani 225 \n9 Rani Rasmi Tank 134 \n10 Kharkhara Tank 6568 \n11 Matiamoti tank 3438 \n12 Sutiyapat Medium project 452 \n13 Kara Nala 296 \n14 Sukha Nala 142 \n TOTAL 62892 \nGoa   \n1 Anjunem 1460 \n TOTAL 1460 \nGujarat   \n1 Sardar Sarovar 18000 \n2 Kadana 16151 \n3 Ukai 16000 \n4 Panam 17491 \n5 Damanganga 11805 \n6 Sipu reservoir 7225 \n7 Wetrak Reservoir 15670 \n8 Sabarmati reserv