    "ls|LS16_S8_U_223": " \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.223 \nFOR ANSWER ON 25/04/2016 \n \nSTEEL CONSUMPTION \n \n223. SHRI VENKATESH BABU T.G.: \n \nWill the Minister of STEEL be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the total quantity of steel produced  and imported for domestic consumption in  \nthe country during each of the last three years; \n \n(b) whether the Government is aware  of the import, sale and storage of cheaper  \nquality of steel not in conformity with  Quality Control Order (QCO), if so, the  details \nthereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government has ta ken any steps to cease the poor quality steel  \nimports and initiated any action against those indulging in such malpractices; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF         (SHRI VISHNU DEO SAI) \nSTEEL AND MINES \n \n(a) Total production & import of steel during the last 3 years is as follows:- \n \nYear Total Finished Steel (million tones) \nProduction of Sale Import \n2013-14 87.67 5.45 \n2014-15 92.16 9.32 \n2015-16* 90.39 11.71 \nSource: JPC: * prov. \n \n(b) After the issue of the quality control orders, import of seconds & defective \nproducts by some unscrupulous importers were reported in respect of some \ncategories of steel products.  However, Government does not maintain data on \nimport, sale and storage of such sub-standard steel products standards-wise. \n \n(c)&(d): Governm ent has notified the following Steel and Steel P roducts ( Quality \nControl) Orders inter-alia to ensure availability of quality steel to end-users. \n \n(i) Steel and Steel Products (Quality Control) Order, 2012. \n(ii) Steel and Steel Products (Quality Control) Second Order, 2012. \n(iii) Steel and Steel Products (Quality Control) Order, 2015. \n \n Further, Government has issued orders to allow import of steel products \nstrictly as per the aforesaid Steel Quality Control Order inter -alia prohibiting import of \nsub-standard steel products not conforming to the relevant Indian Standards. \n \n******** ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_224": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*224 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 10TH MAY, 2016/VAISAKHA 20, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nBORDER MANAGEMENT \n \n*224.  SHRI NINONG ERING: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether adequate measures have  been taken by the Government to \nsecure effective management of Indian borders  particularly in Arunachal \nPradesh and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether the Government has set up/proposes to set up border haats \nalong the Indo-Myanmar and Indo-Bangladesh borders and if so, the details \nthereof, location/State-wise; \n \n(c) whether the border haats are likely  to help in maintaining peace and \ntranquility in the border regions and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) the concrete steps taken/proposed to be taken by the Government to \ncurb insurgency and trafficking problems as well as to maintain peace and \nsecurity in the border regions including Indo-Myanmar border region? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n-2- \n \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*224 \nFOR 10.05.2016. \n \n \n(a) & (b): The Government has adopted a multi-pronged strategy to secure \neffective management of India n borders, curb insurgency as well as to \nmaintain peace and security in the border regions which inter -alia \nincludes, area domination, round the clock surveillance & patrolling on the \nborders, establishment of Border Out Posts (BOPs), construction of border \nroads, upgradation of intelligence set up and close interaction with local \npopulace.   Wherever required and possible on respective borders, fence \nand flood light works are taken up.  Force multip Pliers and High -Tech \nsurveillance equipment to enhance the surveillance of border have also \nbeen introduced.   Further, deployment of technological solutions on Pilot \nbasis has been approved.    Adequate measures are taken to curb human \ntrafficking like issuing advisories to State Gov ernments,  sensitizing law \nenforcement agencies and creating awareness among border population. \n \n(c) & (d):    Four border haats, two in Meghalaya and two in Tripura are \nfunctional at present along Indo-Bangladesh border.   Government of  \n \n…..3/ \n\n \n-3- \nL.S.S.Q.NO.*224 FOR 10.05.2016 \n \nIndia and Bangladesh have agreed to set up six more border haats -two in \nTripura and four in Meghalaya.   There are no border haats at Indo -\nMyanmar border.   The establishment of border haats is expected to \npromote the well being of the people dwelling in areas across the borders \nof the two countries, which in turn will maintain peace and tranquility in \nthe border regions.   \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_226": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *226 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 10.05.2016 \n \nFinancial Assistance for Sports Infrastructure \n \n*226. SHRI ANTO ANTONY: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government is providing financial assistance for setting \nup of Indoor Halls to improve sports infrastructure/facilities in various \nStates;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof including the number of Indoor Halls \ncompleted and pending so far; \n \n(c) whether the Government has released the first instalment for setting \nup an Indoor Hall in Pathanamthitta District, Kerala recently and if so, the \ndetails thereof; and  \n \nd) whether there is a delay in constructing this Indoor Hall and if so, the \ndetails thereof ? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL) \n \n(a) to (d)  A statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PAR TS (a) TO ( d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. * 226 FOR 10.05.2016 ASKED BY SHRI \nANTO ANTONY , MP REGARDING FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE FOR SPORTS \nINFRASTRUCTURE \n(a) & (b) Yes, Madam. The Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports was \nimplementing the Centrally Sponsored Scheme of Rajiv Gandhi Khel \nAbhiyan (RGKA) which, inter -alia, provided for financial assistance to \nStates/UTs for construction of indoors halls. Under the erstwhile RGKA, \nfinancial assistance to the tune of Rs. 1.60 crore was provided for \nconstruction of four indoor halls @Rs.40 lakh each to the States of Andhra \nPradesh for 2 blocks and one block each to Punjab and Tamil Nadu in \nMarch, 2016. Construction of none of these indoor halls has been \ncompleted as yet. \n This Ministry was also implementing t he Urban Sports \nInfrastructure Scheme (USIS), which inter -alia provided for financial \nassistance to States/UTs for setting up of Multipurpose Indoor Halls. The \nState-wise details of multi-purpose Indoor Halls sanctioned from 2010 -11 \nto 2015 -16 are given in  Annexure-I. Out of the sanctioned Indoor Halls, \nconstruction of only one multi-purpose indoor hall at Mualpui, District \nAizawl in the State of Mizoram has been completed.   \n This Ministry has launched the “Khelo India – National Programme \nfor Development of Sports” by merging three erstwhile schemes, namely, \nthe Rajiv Gandhi Khel Abhiyan (RGKA), the Urban Sports Infrastructure \nScheme (USIS) and the National Sports Talent Search Scheme (NSTSS), \ninto an umbrella Central Sector Scheme, to be implemented from 2016-17. \nThis Scheme, inter-alia, provides for financial assistance for setting up of \nMultipurpose Indoor Halls to improve sports infrastructure/facilities in \nvarious States/UTs. \n \n(c) & (d) The Ministry has released the first installment of Rs.1.80 crore \non 02.03.2016 to the State Government of Kerala for Construction of \nmulti-purpose indoor hall at Pathanamthitta, Kerala . The Utilization \nCertificate (UC) for the grant released on 02.03.2016 will become due on \n01.04.2017.  \n****** \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART S (a) & (b) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *226 FOR 10.05.2016 ASKED BY SHRI \nANTO ANTONY, MP REGARDING FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE FOR SPORTS \nINFRASTRUCTURE  \nAnnexure – I \n \nState-wise details of multi-purpose Indoor Halls sanctioned from 2010-11 to 2015-16 \n \n2010-11                                    (Rs. in crore) \nS. \nNo. State Project \nGrant  \nApproved \n(Date) \nGrant  \nReleased \n(Date) \n1. Punjab \n \nConstruction of Multi -purpose Indoor Hall at \nTarn Taran \n3.98 \n(17.03.2011) \n2.00 \n(17.03.2011) \n \n \n2011-12                                      (Rs. in crore) \n \nS.No. State Project \nGrant \napproved \n(Date) \nGrant released \n(Date)  \n1 Rajasthan \n \nConstruction of Multi -purpose Indoor Hall at \